From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 22:53:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] RIL: re-arm the radio proxy after a stale-handle getService
 race

If rild dies between getService() returning and setResponseFunctions(),
the call throws (HwBinder error -32), mRadioProxy stays null and no retry
is scheduled, so telephony is stuck until the phone process is killed.
MediaTek modem init can restart rild at that moment. Replay
EVENT_RADIO_PROXY_DEAD with the current cookie so the handler gets the
service again; a successful attach in the meantime bumps the cookie and
the replay is ignored.
---
 src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RIL.java | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RIL.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RIL.java
index 7352dc5..8c1e3b0 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RIL.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RIL.java
@@ -380,6 +380,15 @@ public class RIL extends BaseCommands implements CommandsInterface {
         } catch (RemoteException | RuntimeException e) {
             mRadioProxy = null;
             riljLoge("RadioProxy getService/setResponseFunctions: " + e);
+            // rild can die between getService() and setResponseFunctions();
+            // without a retry mRadioProxy stays null until the phone process
+            // restarts. Replay the proxy-death event, which gets the service
+            // again; a successful attach in the meantime bumps the cookie and
+            // the replay is ignored.
+            mRilHandler.sendMessageDelayed(
+                    mRilHandler.obtainMessage(EVENT_RADIO_PROXY_DEAD,
+                            mRadioProxyCookie.get()),
+                    IRADIO_GET_SERVICE_DELAY_MILLIS);
         }
 
         if (mRadioProxy == null) {
